The native dispatch is in place:
- one `PythonReceiverRequest` keeps the selected operation for the whole batch, while each point still gets its own bounded session;
- typed open, budget and cancelled statuses survive, along with call evidence;
- no golden changed;
- the hard-won tests #5721, #5745 and #5738 pass unchanged.

Two things need follow-up before I accept it. The child kept "the direct legacy hook as fallback only when no Python analyzer is available". A fallback into the code PR 3 deletes is exactly what the plan forbids, so I'll look at it. And the validation was only focused subsets: 25 policy tests where the full Python set is about 300. The broader suites still need to run.
